docs/design-concepts

# Secrets must not enter the build context. `Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, and the ROOT `.env`
# is the file docker-compose.yml and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md tell every operator to create
# (`cp .env.example .env`) — it holds SECRET_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, ADMIN_SECRET,
# DIVERA_ACCESS_KEY, TRACCAR_PASSWORD, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY and STT_API_KEY. Only `backend/.env`
# was listed here, so a source build baked the real one into an image layer and into any
# exported build cache. The pattern now covers both, and `.env.example` is explicitly kept
# because it is documentation and carries no values.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Same rule, second miss: a STATION's own data must not enter the build context either. These
# paths are all gitignored — they are exactly the things that never belong in the public repo —
# but `.gitignore` has no bearing on the build context, so `COPY . .` baked them into an image
# layer. Verified 2026-08-16 on a `--build` install: backend/private/oberwil.config.json and
# live.config.json were sitting in /app inside the running container. That matters more now that
# `./scripts/setup.sh --build` is a documented path, and it is how one station's config would
# reach another station's image.
backend/private/
public/leitungskataster/
tmp/

# Maintainer-internal working notes. Not secret, but nothing here is needed at runtime and it
# should not ship inside a station's image.
docs/planning/
mockups/
todo.md
